WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.280
Geometry allows a few shapes.

2
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.360
So what chooses among them?

3
00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:09.803
Mostly, water does.

4
00:00:10.823 --> 00:00:13.983
Picture one oily side chain, like leucine's, sitting in water.

5
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:19.947
Water molecules hydrogen bond to each other all the time, in a shifting network.

6
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.430
Next to the oily surface, they cannot hydrogen bond to it.

7
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:29.893
So the water in contact forms a tighter, more ordered network around it, like a

8
00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:30.893
cage.

9
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.137
Ordered water has lost freedom.

10
00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:35.017
That is lost entropy.

11
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.400
Now bring two oily side chains together.

12
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.140
Less oily surface faces the water.

13
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:43.963
Less water has to be caged.

14
00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:47.383
The freed water tumbles away and gains entropy.

15
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.707
That gain drives the oily groups together.

16
00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:53.207
It is called the hydrophobic effect.

17
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.720
A common mistake is that oil is pulled to oil.

18
00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.760
But oily groups attract water about as well.

19
00:01:00.733 --> 00:01:04.813
Oily groups are pushed together by water, not pulled together by each other.

20
00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:10.937
So in a water-soluble protein, the nonpolar side chains end up buried in a core.

21
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.520
Polar and charged side chains sit on the surface, in the water.

22
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:19.013
This packs the whole chain into a compact shape.

23
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:21.113
That is tertiary structure.

24
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.987
Burial also helps explain helices and sheets.

25
00:01:26.007 --> 00:01:28.367
Buried backbone groups lose their water partners.

26
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:32.727
A buried polar group with no partner costs free energy.

27
00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.950
The cheapest fix is for the backbone to bond to itself.

28
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.590
Helices and sheets are the regular ways to do that.

29
00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:43.493
Burial does not stop at one chain.

30
00:01:44.473 --> 00:01:47.413
Folded chains can bury oily surface against each other.

31
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:50.737
That assembly is quaternary structure.

32
00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:55.277
Hemoglobin is two alpha and two beta subunits, working as one.

33
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.947
Now return to sickle cell.

34
00:01:59.007 --> 00:02:02.487
Valine puts an oily residue on the surface, where a charged one was.

35
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.130
That makes a new sticky patch.

36
00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:10.690
Once oxygen is released, the patch fits an oily pocket on a neighbouring hemoglobin.

37
00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:16.750
Sickle cell is an unwanted contact between whole hemoglobins, built by the same

38
00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:17.750
rule.

39
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.210
One more surprise.

40
00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:24.490
A folded protein is only marginally more stable than the unfolded coil.

41
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.960
The chain gives up a lot of freedom to fold.

42
00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.580
Its contacts and freed water only just pay for it.

43
00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:34.103
So heat can undo a fold.

44
00:02:34.943 --> 00:02:38.103
The melting temperature is where half the molecules are unfolded.

45
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:43.077
Here is the test. A buried leucine becomes aspartate.

46
00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:45.997
Or a surface lysine becomes arginine.

47
00:02:46.877 --> 00:02:47.877
Which one melts lower?

48
00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:55.667
The buried aspartate.

49
00:02:56.267 --> 00:03:00.447
It is charged, with no water to bond with, and it breaks up the oily packing.

50
00:03:01.517 --> 00:03:05.457
The surface swap trades one positive charge for another, still in water.

51
00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:07.597
Stability barely changes.

52
00:03:08.717 --> 00:03:10.377
Water pushes oil inward.

53
00:03:10.377 --> 00:03:13.437
That burial builds the core and the interfaces.
